1
00:00:00,360 --> 00:00:03,509
You cowards.

2
00:00:03,510 --> 00:00:07,320
Just shut up and let me shoulder it all!

3
00:00:13,310 --> 00:00:17,619
You don't need to be educated by words.

4
00:00:17,620 --> 00:00:19,120
You need training.

5
00:00:21,100 --> 00:00:23,120
I've made my decision.

6
00:00:23,880 --> 00:00:27,029
Eren was put under the
care of the Recon Corps.

7
00:00:27,030 --> 00:00:29,920
He was to dedicate himself to
missions outside the Wall.

8
00:00:32,570 --> 00:00:33,930
Oh, my friend!

9
00:00:33,933 --> 00:00:36,450
This is a victory for us!

10
00:00:36,510 --> 00:00:38,060
Our fame starts here!

11
00:00:39,650 --> 00:00:40,710
Oh, my friend!

12
00:00:40,713 --> 00:00:45,910
Let us celebrate this victory for the next battle!

13
00:01:00,550 --> 00:01:02,371
"I died for naught"

14
00:01:02,396 --> 00:01:06,110
I won't let it end like that for you.

15
00:01:06,113 --> 00:01:08,900
Until I am the last one standing

16
00:01:11,350 --> 00:01:12,179
The enemy is cruel...

17
00:01:12,204 --> 00:01:14,430
We will kill...

18
00:01:14,433 --> 00:01:17,369
The enemy is colossal... We will jump...

19
00:01:17,370 --> 00:01:21,050
In our hands we hold blades of glory.

20
00:01:21,053 --> 00:01:23,289
And sing in the name of victory

21
00:01:23,290 --> 00:01:25,610
We bear the wings of freedom on our backs

22
00:01:29,250 --> 00:01:32,310
Swearing iron determination upon our hearts,

23
00:01:35,390 --> 00:01:37,650
we slash apart the circle of idiocy

24
00:01:41,490 --> 00:01:43,810
and soar through the sky

25
00:01:43,870 --> 00:01:45,970
With our wings of freedom

26
00:02:01,980 --> 00:02:06,980
Special Operations Squad: Eve of the Counterattack, Part 2

27
00:02:07,540 --> 00:02:12,260
Trost

28
00:02:15,170 --> 00:02:18,759
Former Recon Corps HQ

29
00:02:18,760 --> 00:02:21,490
The former Recon Corps headquarters.

30
00:02:22,960 --> 00:02:26,189
It's nothing more than a renovated old castle.

31
00:02:26,190 --> 00:02:28,920
While it definitely looks impressive,

32
00:02:29,490 --> 00:02:34,019
it's so far from the Walls and all rivers

33
00:02:34,020 --> 00:02:36,880
that it's completely useless
to the Recon Corps.

34
00:02:37,940 --> 00:02:42,559
The story goes back to the ambitious
early days when the Corps was formed.

35
00:02:42,560 --> 00:02:49,060
Who would've thought we'd end up using
it again to serve as your hideout?

36
00:02:52,580 --> 00:02:54,789
Don't get cocky, new blood.

37
00:02:54,790 --> 00:02:55,480
What?

38
00:02:55,980 --> 00:02:58,349
I don't know the deal with this
crap about you being a Titan,

39
00:02:58,350 --> 00:03:02,200
but we can't have Captain Levi babysit...

40
00:03:07,660 --> 00:03:11,149
That's what you get for talking
while riding your horse.

41
00:03:11,150 --> 00:03:13,019
The first moments leave the
most important impression.

42
00:03:13,020 --> 00:03:15,409
That newbie was scared shitless.

43
00:03:15,410 --> 00:03:19,019
I think he was just stunned
silent by how lame you are.

44
00:03:19,020 --> 00:03:22,979
Still, it's all going according to plan.

45
00:03:22,980 --> 00:03:26,640
Man, you never used to talk like that.

46
00:03:27,320 --> 00:03:31,929
If, by chance, you're trying
to imitate Captain Levi,

47
00:03:31,930 --> 00:03:33,939
you should really stop it.

48
00:03:33,940 --> 00:03:37,150
You two are nothing alike, but still...

49
00:03:38,310 --> 00:03:41,139
Do you want to chain me down, Petra?

50
00:03:41,140 --> 00:03:45,160
You're still ways to go to
be fitting for my wife.

51
00:03:45,530 --> 00:03:48,559
If only you'd bled to death
from biting your tongue.

52
00:03:48,560 --> 00:03:51,459
You keep on boasting about how
many Titans you've killed too.

53
00:03:51,460 --> 00:03:56,710
So what? I've boasted about you guys too.

54
00:03:57,360 --> 00:04:01,939
Those people are the Recon
Corps' Special Ops Squad,

55
00:04:01,940 --> 00:04:03,379
commonly known as the Levi Unit.

56
00:04:03,380 --> 00:04:06,099
You're pathetic!

57
00:04:06,100 --> 00:04:11,540
Petra Ral. Took down 10 Titans.
Assisted with taking down another 46.

58
00:04:12,600 --> 00:04:17,190
Auruo Bossard. Took down 39.
Assisted with another 9.

59
00:04:18,020 --> 00:04:19,930
They are the elite of the elite.

60
00:04:22,480 --> 00:04:27,769
Erd Gin. Took down 14.
Assisted with another 32.

61
00:04:27,770 --> 00:04:32,210
Gunther Schultz. Took down 7.
Assisted with another 40.

62
00:04:33,690 --> 00:04:38,559
They are the top tier of the Recon
Corps, hand-picked by Captain Levi.

63
00:04:38,560 --> 00:04:45,410
If I went berserk, these people
would be the ones to kill me.

64
00:04:47,230 --> 00:04:49,180
It's covered in weeds.

65
00:04:49,490 --> 00:04:51,379
It looks terrible.

66
00:04:51,380 --> 00:04:53,859
It's been disused for a very long time.

67
00:04:53,860 --> 00:04:56,019
Inside, a sea of dust is probably awaiting us.

68
00:04:56,020 --> 00:04:59,070
That is indeed a severe problem.

69
00:04:59,760 --> 00:05:02,020
We must sort it out immediately.

70
00:05:10,850 --> 00:05:13,500
We're done cleaning the upper floors.

71
00:05:14,790 --> 00:05:17,630
Where will I get to sleep
in the building, sir?

72
00:05:19,060 --> 00:05:21,130
Your room is in the basement.

73
00:05:21,460 --> 00:05:23,899
The basement again, sir?

74
00:05:23,900 --> 00:05:28,340
Of course. You're not in complete
control of yourself yet.

75
00:05:28,960 --> 00:05:31,079
If you drifted off and turned into a Titan,

76
00:05:31,080 --> 00:05:33,180
at least if you're underground
we can restrain you right away.

77
00:05:33,750 --> 00:05:38,619
That was one of the conditions agreed
upon for us to get custody of you.

78
00:05:38,620 --> 00:05:40,190
It's a rule that we must follow.

79
00:05:42,830 --> 00:05:44,519
I'll take a look around the rooms.

80
00:05:44,520 --> 00:05:46,849
You do this room, Eren.

81
00:05:46,850 --> 00:05:47,700
Yes, sir.

82
00:05:53,650 --> 00:05:55,659
You've got quite a despairing
look on your face, Eren.

83
00:05:55,660 --> 00:05:56,839
I do?

84
00:05:56,840 --> 00:05:59,289
Ah, I'll be calling you Eren.

85
00:05:59,290 --> 00:06:01,439
Captain Levi does the same.

86
00:06:01,440 --> 00:06:03,460
Here, his word is the law.

87
00:06:03,840 --> 00:06:06,949
Right... I don't mind that,

88
00:06:06,950 --> 00:06:09,889
but did I really have a
despairing look on my face?

89
00:06:09,890 --> 00:06:11,720
It's not surprising at all.

90
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:16,359
He doesn't come across as the perfect,
invulnerable hero people think he is, does he?

91
00:06:16,360 --> 00:06:20,909
The true Levi is surprisingly short,

92
00:06:20,910 --> 00:06:23,660
irritable, violent, and hard to approach.

93
00:06:24,230 --> 00:06:31,059
That's not it. I was surprised how obediently
he accepts the decisions of the higher-ups.

94
00:06:31,060 --> 00:06:33,176
Did you think that,
as strong as he is,

95
00:06:33,201 --> 00:06:35,979
he wouldn't care about rank
or the chain of command?

96
00:06:35,980 --> 00:06:37,250
Yes.

97
00:06:37,460 --> 00:06:40,989
I expected him not to
acquiesce to anyone's words.

98
00:06:40,990 --> 00:06:46,260
I don't know the details myself, but I heard
he was pretty much like that originally.

99
00:06:47,390 --> 00:06:53,670
Before joining the Recon Corps, he was a
famous thug in the capital's underworld.

100
00:06:54,860 --> 00:06:57,269
But then, why?

101
00:06:57,270 --> 00:07:01,139
I don't know exactly what happened.

102
00:07:01,140 --> 00:07:06,170
He was taken in to the Recon Corps
under Commander Erwin's hands.

103
00:07:07,210 --> 00:07:08,450
The Commander?

104
00:07:09,030 --> 00:07:10,529
Hey, Eren!

105
00:07:10,530 --> 00:07:12,569
Yes, sir?

106
00:07:12,570 --> 00:07:16,290
It's no good at all. Redo it all from scratch.

107
00:07:18,630 --> 00:07:19,635
So, in thirty days,

108
00:07:19,660 --> 00:07:22,674
we're to go outside the Walls to build
a stronghold for the supply chain?

109
00:07:23,540 --> 00:07:26,650
Not to mention we'll be taking
fresh graduates with us too.

110
00:07:27,120 --> 00:07:29,550
If we even get any new recruits that is.

111
00:07:30,760 --> 00:07:35,010
In my opinion, this is far too hasty.

112
00:07:35,580 --> 00:07:39,359
Eren's current position is a temporary thing.

113
00:07:39,360 --> 00:07:44,940
We must quickly and smoothly
prove his usefulness to Central.

114
00:07:45,750 --> 00:07:49,679
Otherwise, sooner or later, the
Police will make another move to...

115
00:07:49,680 --> 00:07:52,610
Can't you take that mask off
at least for me, Erwin?

116
00:07:58,170 --> 00:08:01,120
You're really good at sniffing
out things like this, Mike.

117
00:08:02,290 --> 00:08:05,040
Too bad you have no scent whatsoever.

118
00:08:06,310 --> 00:08:08,270
I'll tell you when the time is right.

119
00:08:15,980 --> 00:08:20,099
We'll probably be ordered to
stand by for a few more days,

120
00:08:20,100 --> 00:08:24,439
but I heard we're supposed to be going
on a large-scale extramural expedition.

121
00:08:24,440 --> 00:08:28,689
And we'll be taking the new
graduates with us as well.

122
00:08:28,690 --> 00:08:30,879
Is this true, Erd?

123
00:08:30,880 --> 00:08:32,650
Isn't it awfully soon?

124
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:37,950
Even considering that they handled
this last Titan attack quite well...

125
00:08:38,280 --> 00:08:41,719
I heard those kids' pants required multiple
washings to remove the shitstains.

126
00:08:41,720 --> 00:08:43,119
Is this all true, Captain?

127
00:08:43,120 --> 00:08:46,789
I'm not involved in making our plans.

128
00:08:46,790 --> 00:08:51,629
It's Erwin. He's likely considering far
more variables that might occur to us.

129
00:08:51,630 --> 00:08:56,019
It's true that we're in an
unprecedented situation.

130
00:08:56,020 --> 00:08:59,370
On the one hand, we lost
the Maria reconquest route

131
00:08:59,395 --> 00:09:02,269
that we established
through huge sacrifices,

132
00:09:02,270 --> 00:09:05,350
but on the other hand, we got
an unexpected ray of hope.

133
00:09:13,900 --> 00:09:16,589
I still have trouble believing it.

134
00:09:16,590 --> 00:09:20,370
You can "turn into a Titan",
but what's that mean, Eren?

135
00:09:21,200 --> 00:09:25,009
My memories from that time are quite hazy.

136
00:09:25,010 --> 00:09:27,519
It felt like a selfless, dreaming state.

137
00:09:27,520 --> 00:09:30,909
It can be triggered by hurting myself.

138
00:09:30,910 --> 00:09:32,250
Like, if I bite...

139
00:09:32,620 --> 00:09:37,360
Wait, how do I know this?

140
00:09:38,320 --> 00:09:40,589
You guys know all of this too.

141
00:09:40,590 --> 00:09:43,449
We couldn't get any more out of him
than what's written in the reports.

142
00:09:43,450 --> 00:09:46,510
She won't stay put though.

143
00:09:48,980 --> 00:09:53,809
Her meddling could even kill you, Eren.

144
00:09:53,810 --> 00:09:55,720
She? Who?

145
00:10:00,370 --> 00:10:04,080
Good evening, gentlemen of the Levi Unit!

146
00:10:04,310 --> 00:10:06,959
Have you made yourselves
at home in the castle?

147
00:10:06,960 --> 00:10:08,299
You're early.

148
00:10:08,300 --> 00:10:10,579
How could I stay put now?

149
00:10:10,580 --> 00:10:12,659
Major Hanji?

150
00:10:12,660 --> 00:10:14,339
Sorry for the wait, Eren.

151
00:10:14,340 --> 00:10:20,039
I'm charged with experimenting on the
two Titans we caught alive in the city.

152
00:10:20,040 --> 00:10:23,099
I want you to help me out
with tomorrow's experiments.

153
00:10:23,100 --> 00:10:25,309
I came to ask permission for that.

154
00:10:25,310 --> 00:10:27,600
An experiment?

155
00:10:28,050 --> 00:10:29,179
What am I supposed to...

156
00:10:29,180 --> 00:10:33,730
What else but that totally
awesome thing you do!

157
00:10:34,070 --> 00:10:38,280
Uh... I can't give you permission myself.

158
00:10:38,920 --> 00:10:42,109
I don't have authority over myself, you see.

159
00:10:42,110 --> 00:10:44,410
Levi, what are Eren's plans for tomorrow?

160
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:46,289
Cleaning the garden.

161
00:10:46,290 --> 00:10:48,790
Okay then, it's decided!

162
00:10:50,720 --> 00:10:52,920
I'll be counting on you tomorrow, Eren!

163
00:10:54,010 --> 00:10:55,130
Yes, ma'am.

164
00:10:55,660 --> 00:10:59,049
But what exactly are these
experiments on the Titans?

165
00:10:59,050 --> 00:10:59,300
Hm?

166
00:11:00,870 --> 00:11:03,930
Uh... What exactly are these experiments...

167
00:11:04,170 --> 00:11:05,850
Stop that. Don't ask her.

168
00:11:07,230 --> 00:11:09,129
Ah, I knew it.

169
00:11:09,130 --> 00:11:12,230
You just had this expression
like you wanted to know.

170
00:11:23,450 --> 00:11:25,939
Were you that interested?

171
00:11:25,940 --> 00:11:27,580
Then I've got no choice.

172
00:11:28,110 --> 00:11:30,540
I guess I've gotta tell you

173
00:11:31,320 --> 00:11:35,460
what I know about those
pretties we caught earlier.

174
00:11:36,000 --> 00:11:38,092
Currently Disclosable Information: The Wall
Faith (pt 1) A religious sect with growing

175
00:11:38,117 --> 00:11:39,476
influence in the inner lands.
They worship the Walls and

176
00:11:39,501 --> 00:11:40,930
won't allow anyone to touch them,
even for defense purposes.

177
00:11:40,933 --> 00:11:43,204
Currently Disclosable Information: The
Wall Faith (2) Since the fall of Wall

178
00:11:43,229 --> 00:11:45,824
Maria, the number of their followers is
growing rapidly, and so does their influence.

179
00:11:47,130 --> 00:11:50,510
First, we repeated the experiments
we'd done each of the five

180
00:11:50,535 --> 00:11:52,714
prior times we had
Titans to play with.

181
00:11:55,170 --> 00:11:56,150
Hello.

182
00:11:59,160 --> 00:12:02,510
First, we attempted communication.

183
00:12:03,100 --> 00:12:06,289
How are you feeling? What's your name?

184
00:12:06,290 --> 00:12:07,580
Does it hurt anywhere?

185
00:12:08,220 --> 00:12:10,320
Major, you're too close!

186
00:12:12,780 --> 00:12:13,790
Hello.

187
00:12:14,610 --> 00:12:16,059
Isn't the weather wonderful today?

188
00:12:16,060 --> 00:12:16,840
Are you hungry?

189
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:20,099
Whoa!

190
00:12:20,100 --> 00:12:20,950
Whoa-whoa, that was close!

191
00:12:20,951 --> 00:12:22,999
Major, it's too dangerous!

192
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:29,210
Sadly, communication proved
impossible this time as well.

193
00:12:31,300 --> 00:12:36,839
But for me, interacting with
the Titans was so enlightening

194
00:12:36,840 --> 00:12:38,820
that it made me entirely
forget my everyday fatigue.

195
00:12:39,990 --> 00:12:45,110
A long, long time ago, there
was a tribe who ate people.

196
00:12:46,390 --> 00:12:51,259
They weren't Titans like you.
They were humans.

197
00:12:51,260 --> 00:12:54,670
They hid out in caves in the mountains,

198
00:12:54,950 --> 00:12:57,959
attacked travelers who happened
to tread the roads nearby,

199
00:12:57,960 --> 00:12:59,039
robbed them of their valuables,

200
00:12:59,040 --> 00:13:00,259
killed them,

201
00:13:00,260 --> 00:13:02,400
and ate their flesh.

202
00:13:02,890 --> 00:13:06,539
She's started another one
of her naming ceremonies.

203
00:13:06,540 --> 00:13:09,219
What did we end up with last time?

204
00:13:09,220 --> 00:13:11,179
Chicacchironi and Albert.

205
00:13:11,180 --> 00:13:16,959
They kept up their resistance for 25 years.

206
00:13:16,960 --> 00:13:22,229
During that time, over 500
people became their prey.

207
00:13:22,230 --> 00:13:26,250
That might be more than
the humans you guys ate.

208
00:13:26,900 --> 00:13:30,990
They also experimented with various
ways of preparing their meals.

209
00:13:31,330 --> 00:13:33,450
Turning the buttocks into steaks.

210
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:37,389
Cutting the thighs up into cubes
and cooking a stew with them.

211
00:13:37,390 --> 00:13:41,189
They minced, kneaded, and fried the hard meat.

212
00:13:41,190 --> 00:13:44,590
Out of fat and innards,
they even made sausages.

213
00:13:44,960 --> 00:13:48,840
That's right. They knew
the concept of "cooking".

214
00:13:49,220 --> 00:13:51,850
That's how they were different from you.

215
00:13:52,390 --> 00:13:58,850
But then those cannibals made a mistake,
and they were all caught and executed.

216
00:13:59,120 --> 00:14:01,869
That's the same as you.

217
00:14:01,870 --> 00:14:05,559
You made the mistake of attacking mankind,

218
00:14:05,560 --> 00:14:07,250
and you were caught.

219
00:14:08,990 --> 00:14:14,800
So I'll name you after the
man who led that clan.

220
00:14:15,450 --> 00:14:17,020
You're Sawney.

221
00:14:17,330 --> 00:14:19,260
You're Bean.

222
00:14:20,540 --> 00:14:25,590
But don't worry. I won't have you executed.

223
00:14:26,200 --> 00:14:27,510
Nice to meet you, Sawney.

224
00:14:28,110 --> 00:14:29,430
You too, Bean.

225
00:14:30,740 --> 00:14:32,640
Let's try to get along.

226
00:14:34,070 --> 00:14:40,680
Thus I named the 7 meter class Bean,
and the 4 meter class Sawney.

227
00:14:45,450 --> 00:14:49,339
Next we tried denying them sunlight.

228
00:14:49,340 --> 00:14:52,659
The Titans are clearly less
active during the night.

229
00:14:52,660 --> 00:14:57,660
These experiments tried to prove that they
gain some kind of power from the sunlight.

230
00:14:58,490 --> 00:15:01,860
There was a huge variation
between individual Titans.

231
00:15:03,770 --> 00:15:05,420
You've worked hard, Sawney.

232
00:15:06,380 --> 00:15:08,970
Good night. See you tomorrow.

233
00:15:09,740 --> 00:15:15,279
Sawney's activity dropped an hour after
we denied them sunlight. In contrast...

234
00:15:15,280 --> 00:15:19,489
You really like to stay up late, huh, Bean?

235
00:15:19,490 --> 00:15:22,940
It's okay. I'll stay here with you.

236
00:15:23,990 --> 00:15:26,880
Bean stayed lively for three hours.

237
00:15:30,200 --> 00:15:32,450
They always manage to surprise me.

238
00:15:32,720 --> 00:15:35,389
They don't need water or food.

239
00:15:35,390 --> 00:15:39,019
They have vocal organs, yet
they don't need to breathe.

240
00:15:39,020 --> 00:15:42,460
All they need to stay alive is sunlight.

241
00:15:42,880 --> 00:15:45,739
To be honest, I'm curious what would
happen if we denied them sunlight completely,

242
00:15:45,740 --> 00:15:49,340
but they're such valuable experimental
subjects, I can't risk them dying.

243
00:15:49,600 --> 00:15:53,580
We killed the previous
captures by accident.

244
00:15:54,200 --> 00:15:58,350
I accidentally hit the nape of the
neck when we tried cutting their heads off.

245
00:15:58,660 --> 00:16:02,390
Their names were
Chicacchironi and Albert.

246
00:16:03,020 --> 00:16:05,340
They had such beautiful smiles.

247
00:16:05,920 --> 00:16:09,380
I feel bad about what I did to them.

248
00:16:11,280 --> 00:16:14,670
I don't want that to
happen again... I'm sorry.

249
00:16:16,380 --> 00:16:18,540
Major Hanji...

250
00:16:20,580 --> 00:16:21,949
And then,

251
00:16:21,950 --> 00:16:28,380
I moved on to the next stage, testing their
sense of pain by actually touching them!

252
00:16:34,640 --> 00:16:37,239
Major, you shouldn't be the one screaming...

253
00:16:37,240 --> 00:16:38,760
How could I not scream, doing this?!

254
00:16:40,520 --> 00:16:42,430
Bean is in so much pain!

255
00:16:43,040 --> 00:16:47,650
Don't give up, Bean! Hang in there!

256
00:16:48,570 --> 00:16:53,860
We had to confirm whether they had any
weaknesses besides the nape of the neck.

257
00:16:54,870 --> 00:16:56,880
It was really tough work.

258
00:16:59,210 --> 00:17:05,479
Sawney? I just pierced your heart.
Doesn't it hurt?

259
00:17:05,480 --> 00:17:06,580
How does it feel?

260
00:17:07,720 --> 00:17:11,090
Compared to Bean, Sawney was a lot quieter.

261
00:17:11,460 --> 00:17:14,060
He hardly reacted at all.

262
00:17:14,910 --> 00:17:18,260
Hm? What was that?

263
00:17:20,990 --> 00:17:23,079
Major, fall back!

264
00:17:23,080 --> 00:17:27,069
Haha, that was really close!

265
00:17:27,070 --> 00:17:28,940
You're gonna end up actually dying!

266
00:17:30,200 --> 00:17:34,779
Sawney isn't very good at expressing himself.

267
00:17:34,780 --> 00:17:37,309
He just keeps trying to bite my head off.

268
00:17:37,310 --> 00:17:39,280
Um, Major Hanji...

269
00:17:40,460 --> 00:17:45,580
How can you stay so carefree
in front of the Titans?

270
00:17:47,720 --> 00:17:53,800
They're our natural enemies, who
drove us to the brink of extinction.

271
00:17:54,210 --> 00:17:58,750
I'm sure you've had to face their threat
a number of times before yourself too.

272
00:18:00,030 --> 00:18:01,499
That's right.

273
00:18:01,500 --> 00:18:05,810
I've had countless comrades murdered
by them right in front of my eyes.

274
00:18:06,830 --> 00:18:11,970
Back when I joined the Recon Corps,
I fought them, fueled by hate.

275
00:18:12,920 --> 00:18:16,320
But then one day I realized...

276
00:18:17,340 --> 00:18:21,240
It was when I cut off and kicked
the head of a 3-meter class.

277
00:18:22,780 --> 00:18:25,290
It was light. Unnaturally so.

278
00:18:25,960 --> 00:18:28,000
Their bodies are light.

279
00:18:29,610 --> 00:18:36,340
Normally such huge bodies shouldn't even
be able to stand and walk on two legs.

280
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:39,439
It's the same with every Titan.

281
00:18:39,440 --> 00:18:44,720
Their cut-off body parts were much lighter
than they should have been for their size.

282
00:18:45,160 --> 00:18:51,400
I heard that when you turned into a Titan,
that body appeared out of thin air.

283
00:18:53,340 --> 00:19:02,200
I considered that maybe the things we see
are not the things that are actually there.

284
00:19:06,630 --> 00:19:12,160
I tried fighting the Titans
out of hatred for decades.

285
00:19:13,040 --> 00:19:17,940
Now I want to try looking at them from a
different point of view than everyone else.

286
00:19:18,990 --> 00:19:21,430
It might prove to be futile.

287
00:19:21,960 --> 00:19:22,800
But still,

288
00:19:23,710 --> 00:19:25,230
I'll do it.

289
00:19:32,620 --> 00:19:36,580
Since I entered the Recon
Corps, all I get are surprises.

290
00:19:37,140 --> 00:19:39,169
It's not just Major Hanji.

291
00:19:39,170 --> 00:19:40,780
They're all weirdos.

292
00:19:41,200 --> 00:19:44,460
It's like a haven for freaks.

293
00:19:44,800 --> 00:19:49,559
But it's also a group of
people who demand change.

294
00:19:49,560 --> 00:19:51,860
That is the Recon Corps.

295
00:19:52,920 --> 00:19:53,790
Major Hanji,

296
00:19:55,050 --> 00:19:59,549
would you be so kind as to tell
me more about your experiments?

297
00:19:59,550 --> 00:20:01,279
Really?

298
00:20:01,280 --> 00:20:05,231
Yes. I think it might prove useful
in tomorrow's experiments

299
00:20:05,256 --> 00:20:07,109
if I learn as much as I can.

300
00:20:07,110 --> 00:20:13,559
Right... I did skip over some of
the details in my summary earlier.

301
00:20:13,560 --> 00:20:15,309
Let me tell you everything then.

302
00:20:15,310 --> 00:20:17,449
It may end up taking quite a while though.

303
00:20:17,450 --> 00:20:18,320
That's fine.

304
00:20:18,321 --> 00:20:23,660
When we first captured a
Titan, I made a hypothesis.

305
00:20:26,300 --> 00:20:31,330
So you've learned nothing new
from what I told you, right?

306
00:20:31,660 --> 00:20:37,340
You should have learned all this as a Cadet.
You knew it all, right?

307
00:20:37,990 --> 00:20:40,859
Yes. There was nothing new.

308
00:20:40,860 --> 00:20:46,230
So let's go over it again, and this time I'll
add my personal opinions and assumptions!

309
00:20:47,240 --> 00:20:48,379
Um, I think we...

310
00:20:48,380 --> 00:20:49,180
First of all, the Tita...

311
00:20:50,190 --> 00:20:51,810
Is Major Hanji here?!

312
00:20:52,750 --> 00:20:54,399
The experiment subjects...

313
00:20:54,400 --> 00:20:57,020
Both of the Titans were killed!

314
00:21:06,590 --> 00:21:09,030
Sawney! Bean!

315
00:21:09,450 --> 00:21:11,199
This can't be for real!

316
00:21:11,200 --> 00:21:13,370
Someone tell me I'm dreaming!

317
00:21:15,200 --> 00:21:18,989
Those experimental subjects were
very valuable. Was it a soldier?

318
00:21:18,990 --> 00:21:21,510
Yes. The culprits are still unknown.

319
00:21:22,290 --> 00:21:25,199
Both Titans were killed before sunrise.

320
00:21:25,200 --> 00:21:29,379
When a guard spotted them, they
escaped using their 3D Maneuver Gear.

321
00:21:29,380 --> 00:21:32,520
So it was a premeditated
move by at least two people?

322
00:21:32,900 --> 00:21:34,699
Sawney!

323
00:21:34,700 --> 00:21:38,770
Check it out! Major Hanji is losing her shit.

324
00:21:40,440 --> 00:21:43,019
What on Earth...

325
00:21:43,020 --> 00:21:46,039
Let's go. This is the
jurisdiction of the Police.

326
00:21:46,040 --> 00:21:47,620
Yes, sir...

327
00:21:50,830 --> 00:21:52,900
What do you see there?

328
00:21:55,430 --> 00:21:57,210
Who do you think is the enemy?

329
00:21:58,040 --> 00:21:59,110
Excuse me?

330
00:22:01,870 --> 00:22:05,050
Sorry, don't mind me.

331
00:22:36,200 --> 00:22:41,590
If we suppose that I am not me,

332
00:22:41,590 --> 00:22:46,130
Can you say with certainty that you are you?

333
00:22:46,780 --> 00:22:51,660
Will you be able to pick up after yourself

334
00:22:51,660 --> 00:22:56,810
Once your sand-like shell breaks and your heart crumbles?

335
00:22:57,090 --> 00:23:02,020
I could hear someone calling

336
00:23:02,310 --> 00:23:05,920
But now my ears are just ringing

337
00:23:06,240 --> 00:23:11,080
It's as if time has frozen

338
00:23:11,380 --> 00:23:13,990
Now, wake up

339
00:23:13,990 --> 00:23:18,960
I began to walk through a deep dark abyss

340
00:23:19,510 --> 00:23:24,260
As swift as a gale, I escaped for my life

341
00:23:24,670 --> 00:23:28,830
I felt like a living corpse

342
00:23:29,240 --> 00:23:33,960
We break out of our walls

343
00:23:34,270 --> 00:23:40,350
To reunite in worlds we've yet to map

344
00:23:53,328 --> 00:23:57,533
While the search for Sawney and Bean's murderers is carried out,

345
00:23:57,933 --> 00:24:01,133
Mikasa, Armin, and the other recruits of the 104th Training Corps

346
00:24:01,333 --> 00:24:05,260
decide which military faction to enlist in, shouldering their own emotions.

347
00:24:05,260 --> 00:24:05,955
What Needs to Be Done Now: Eve of the Counterattack, Part 3
decide which military faction to enlist in, shouldering their own emotions.

348
00:24:05,955 --> 00:24:06,970
What Needs to Be Done Now: Eve of the Counterattack, Part 3
